Kvasir patch: libc include/inttypes.h
Why:       g++ in C++ mode: libc++ imports the C library into std with `using ::name _LIBCPP_USING_IF_EXISTS`;
           clang skips a missing name, gcc has no using_if_exists, so every name libc++ mentions must be
           declared. The Kvasir-owned include/__gcc-compat/inttypes.h (owned.txt) declares the ones this libc
           does not build (declarations only: a call fails at link).
Upstream:  none - Kvasir builds llvm-libc + libc++ with gcc, an upstream-unsupported combination.
Proof:     any gcc build on llvm-libc (`just compiler=gcc libs=llvm build`, the *_gcc_llvm trees) of a file
           that includes <cinttypes> fails without it.
Drop when: gcc is no longer built against llvm-libc, or upstream libc++ supports gcc on llvm-libc.

--- a/include/inttypes.h
+++ b/include/inttypes.h
@@ -26,4 +26,8 @@
 
 __END_C_DECLS
 
+#if defined(__cplusplus) && !defined(__clang__)
+#include "__gcc-compat/inttypes.h"
+#endif
+
 #endif // _LLVM_LIBC_INTTYPES_H
